    "debrief":  {
                    "realTeam":  "In 2014 and 2015, Opportunity\u0027s flash memory (the part that remembers things overnight) started to fail. The rover kept forgetting its data and restarting, which the team called \u0027amnesia\u0027. They told it to use only its short-term memory. That meant it had to send its data to Earth every day before shutting down for the night. Opportunity kept exploring until 2018.",
                    "tryNext":  "Keep the Radio on and send a report every day. Fix the rover quickly so your trips outside stay short.",
                    "realScience":  {
                                        "title":  "Short-term and long-term memory",
                                        "text":  "Computers have fast memory that is wiped when the power turns off, and slower memory that keeps data overnight. Opportunity lost the overnight kind, so it had to send everything home before going to sleep.",
                                        "glossary":  ""
                                    },
